                            <comment id="17739459" author="JIRAUSER297438" created="Mon, 3 Jul 2023 06:34:04 +0000"  >&lt;h1&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;Design%EF%BC%9A&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Design&#65306;&lt;/h1&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Since the components of the dn obtained in the org.springframework.security.ldap.userdetails.LdapUserDetailsMapper#mapUserFromContext method are all lowercase, it cannot be matched with the dn of the native LDAP user called by Kylin through the API, and the spring framework natively obtains It is the case of the key to obtain the dn through the system, and the default is lowercase&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;image-wrap&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/attachment/13061028/13061028_image-2023-07-03-14-33-19-505.png&quot; style=&quot;border: 0px solid black&quot; /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Therefore, in the KylinPropertySourceConfiguration.java code, the configuration prefixed with kylin.system.property. in the kylin.properties file is added to the system configuration, so that the spring framework can read the configuration&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;image-wrap&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/attachment/13061029/13061029_image-2023-07-03-14-33-56-559.png&quot; style=&quot;border: 0px solid black&quot; /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
